<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qishn</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qishn is a coastal town in Al Mahrah <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a> in eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. It was the mainland seat of the Mahra Sultanate of Qishn and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/socotra">Socotra</a>, ruled by the Afrar family, until the sultanate was abolished in 1967 and absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-yemen">South Yemen</a>. The sultans moved between Qishn and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadibu">Hadibu</a> on Socotra.</p></div>
